  "brief": "# Refugee arrivals by US state, 2005-2015\n\n## The story I want to tell\n\nWhich US states took in the most refugees between 2005 and 2015, relative to how many\npeople live there? Raw arrival counts just track how big a place is, so I need a rate that\nlets me compare a small state against a large one fairly.\n\n## The output I need\n\nOne row per state, ranked by arrivals per 1,000 residents, highest first.\n\n| column | type | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `state` | str | the state the refugees were resettled in |\n| `pop_est_2014` | int | 2014 resident population estimate |\n| `arrivals` | int | total refugee arrivals over the whole 2005-2015 period |\n| `per_1k_residents` | float | `arrivals * 1000 / pop_est_2014` |\n\n## Files\n\n- `WRAPS-arrivals-by-destination-2005-2015-clean.csv` - one row per\n  year / origin country / destination state / destination city, with an `arrivals` count.\n- `census-state-populations.csv` - `state`, `pop_est_2014`.\n- `WRAPS-arrivals-by-religion-2005-2015-clean.csv` - the same arrivals broken down by\n  religion instead of destination. Not needed for the table above; included because it\n  covers the same arrivals and may be useful.\n\nSources: US State Department Refugee Processing Center (WRAPS); US Census Bureau.\n",
